+## Forms (FRM)
+
+The forms of the UX baseline review's first pull request (docs/adr/0077): a refused form keeps what the person typed
+but its secrets, names each refused field by the label the person sees, marks it in words and width as well as color,
+moves focus by one rule, keeps its button while it works, and sizes its controls for a phone; a press after a dropped
+connection never saves twice, and what one person typed is never sent as another's.
+
+| ID | Case | Assertion |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| FRM-01 | A refused form keeps what was typed | Text, a select, a text area, a checkbox, a checkbox group, a radio, a date and a month keep the person's values after a refusal, and a valid default never replaces a refused value; a password and a one-time code are emptied, and a note under each says so, asking a locked account for nothing; the action's state carries no value the person typed; a dropped connection keeps every value but the secrets, says the save is not confirmed and which values to type again, and every later press sends the request key of the dropped press until one is saved, even after the page is read again, so nothing is saved twice; a request key used before reads "Already sent", never "Not done", in the neutral notice's look, never the failure colour; a page whose CSRF token or request key is out of date is read again in place, and a second press saves with the values intact; a page read again that shows another person signed in, or no one, clears a form that holds what was typed, says so and invites no press |
+| FRM-02 | A saved form starts fresh | After a success that redirects to the same page, to the same address or to another page, the form shows its defaults, shows no refusal and carries a new request key |
+| FRM-03 | A press while the form is working | Two presses in one frame, a second click and Enter in a field each send one request; the button keeps focus, is aria-disabled and keeps its words; a polite status beside it says "Working…" |
+| FRM-04 | A refused field is named, described and marked | The summary is first in the form, on a line of its own, under "Not done"; its lead is "Fix the field listed here, then try again." for one field, "Fix the fields listed here, then try again." for several, and absent when no issue names a field; each item names its field by the label the person sees (a trailing parenthetical dropped unless it says posted or deposited; a group by its legend, a single box by its own label), links to it, and never shows a key; an issue with no field shows its message alone; under the field, "Error:" beside the message, the element that describes the field holding the message alone; the control is aria-invalid with a 2 px border in the danger color; the same refusal twice is announced twice |
+| FRM-05 | Focus after a refusal | One issue on a field focuses that field; several issues, an issue with no field, a refusal with no issue, a dropped connection, a page out of date or a form cleared for another person focus the summary; a link in the summary focuses its field; the focused element is never under the sticky header |
